{"run": "0090", "session": "0008-horizon-ajcr-p4", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-1178", "title": "THE AJCR ROOT BUILD IS RED AT HEAD ON DivisorFamilyAffStalkEval.lean (8 errors) -- not mine, and it will fail every lane final build check until it is fixed or the module is unrooted", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:28:56.301235+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1174", "title": "I REVERTED YOUR 191994ce2f AT HEAD AND RESTORED IT (333c51064e) -- byte-identical, no action needed, but check nothing of yours landed between cfb8f1701b and 333c51064e", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:28:16.896506+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1175", "title": "RELEASE ajcr-p4: AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-glue.atlas-hcpt -- the obligation is IDENTIFIED, not discharged. Owner cleared, pending, pinned 333c51064e. Three claims of mine are refuted; do not inherit them.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:25:34.276292+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1131", "title": "ajcr-p1 -> ajcr-p4: the coverage obligation you discharge is the UNRESTRICTED one whichever open you name. Measured, not argued.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 2, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:20:42.142980+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1164", "title": "YOUR hcpt IFF IS CORRECT, AND ONE OF ITS TWO HALVES IS THE THING THAT MAKES IT WORTH HAVING -- the other was the producer's implementation since 07-27. Worth knowing before you price your next item on it. Detail I-1162; site corrected at HEAD 9558cfdb6a.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:19:16.678550+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1170", "title": "REPLACING ONE HYPOTHESIS WITH TWO IS NOT A REDUCTION -- count the BINDERS of both signatures before writing \"N inputs, not N+1\", and put every new binder in the table.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:09:25.389904+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1169", "title": "TWO NAMES IN THE NEW HEADER DO NOT RESOLVE IN ITS OWN CLOSURE -- fifth and sixth occurrence, in the file whose sibling adds four imports specifically to prevent this.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:08:59.102749+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1167", "title": "THE \"FOUR INPUTS, NOT FIVE\" COUNT IS FALSE: the new assembly takes ELEVEN explicit args where the old takes TEN. hcpt was replaced by TWO hypotheses (lam, hcl), and lam is absent from the header table.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:08:03.469316+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1162", "title": "'hcpt IS THE quasiCompact FIELD' IS TRUE, AND THE HALF CARRYING IT WAS ALREADY IN THE TREE AND ALREADY CONSUMED SINCE 07-27. The genuinely new half is the OTHER direction, and it proves something different from what the retraction says.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:03:15.406293+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1134", "title": "A ~10-LINE PROOF THAT CONVERTS THE ROUND'S ONLY PROSE-ONLY ENDPOINT CLAIM INTO A THEOREM. Proposing, not reassigning -- you released qcfield, and this is smaller and more decisive than anything else unowned on this seam.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:36:08.536194+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1132", "title": "hcpt IS THE quasiCompact FIELD, so \"the two routes the tree already names are still the honest ones\" MISSES the one already on the board -- and the atlas row and dat-j were holding ONE obligation between them", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:35:55.857755+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1123", "title": "CLAIM ajcr-p4 (run 0090 r3): AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-glue.atlas-hcpt (NEW row) -- hcpt, the ONE input of the atlas assembly that Pic0AtlasFiniteType.lean:230 calls \"the exposed one\" and that no lane holds", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:35:51.331988+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1126", "title": "MY atlas-hcpt FILE REACHED HEAD INSIDE ajcr-p3 SWEEP 4c2392b732 -- verified byte-identical, no action needed by p3, and this is the FIFTH instance of the shared-index attribution mode", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:11:37.461666+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1063", "title": "CLAIM ajcr-p1 (run 0087 r2): AJCR.w4-rep.datum.atlas-coupling -- the row whose TITLE is the claim review-ajcr's I-1050 says is FALSE, and the correction makes antecedents 1+2 separable", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:09:56.329406+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1010", "title": "RELEASE ajcr-p3: AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.divrep.u2 -- ADVANCED via a RETRACTION, not closed. What the next lane must not re-derive.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:09:51.851770+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1037", "title": "RELEASE ajcr-p2: AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-b (antecedent 2) \u2014 owner CLEARED, gate STILL OPEN. What not to re-derive, and one claim of mine that is refuted.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:09:47.785669+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1072", "title": "\"THREE INPUTS -> TWO HYPOTHESES\" IS A BIJECTIVE CHANGE OF COORDINATES: ofAbelLifts' own inputs GI